  "scope": "# Review \u2014 506e262f9354\n\nAssignment `review-081731f2df165db4`; source family `training:db3e9e38`; canonical generator version `3.0.0`, SHA-256 `762a30ac71d7bb9e779a6ce0948247878740259cac499842ef991e2863f20ec5`.\nNeed \u2192 repair: the approved canonical family lacked the requested small rule extension; added a separate proposed `expansion_direction = up | down` episode prototype, focused tests, documentation, and replayable evidence.\nReference rule changes: **none**. `up` is the exact canonical Racket text, raw SHA-256 `7d00cd1a50d3b572eb7a50d096cb5d01f0e7af4d8f9bc403d42a3b905b20dc6f`, normalized SHA-256 `d19e95f77d5885c5260cba5116f1e11ac22936e2f6ef2b2162ea29179885b749`.\nThe alternative `down` setting preserves the same vertical source, endpoint/apex choice, clipped triangular growth, horizontal 7/8 parity, and zero-outside rule while reversing expansion direction.\nRetained seed-17 evidence has 2 fixed-setting episodes, 3 demonstrations + 4 distinct queries each, 14 protected-Racket labels, all 6 canonical labels matched, and zero surviving declared rivals.\nFocused canonical plus prototype tests: **74 passed in 12.20s**. The bridge-reuse regression was observed red first (`write_evidence ignored its supplied bridge`) and then green.\nAdversarial pass: 9 seed/difficulty combinations, 63 distinct inputs, 240 Racket evaluations, exact-type/count rejection, bounded retries, public/private isolation, and max 8-demo/8-query support; no changed-scope defect found.\nSupplementary tickets: tool-policy request reproduced from retained assets and accepted for shared backlog; peer parameter evidence passed count/content-ID privacy checks while its previously declared physical writer-order correction remains pending.\nRemaining limits: finite rival evidence is not proof against every hypothesis; the variant is proposed/unapproved; repeated construction of shared `RacketBridge` instances can stall and remains outside this task's allowed edit scope.\nAssessment: changed scope complete; maintainer attention is needed only for variant review/approval and the separate shared-runtime lifecycle feedback. No production approval or training-admission change is claimed.",
